{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1236881-thoughts-on-the-world","id":1236881,"title":"Thoughts on 'The World'","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-19T13:41:06-07:00","id":1236881,"title":"Thoughts on 'The World'","content":"So I finally got around to reading the Origins pdf and I've only just read through the setting and the explanation of The World. I want to see how others feel about it because I'm not sure how I do. I'll also preface all this by saying I'm aware that you can just make up your own setting if you don't like the one in the book and what not. I also don't dislike what I've read so far. But maybe I need to re-read it or get other people's opinions on it. <br /> <br /> Reading through the description of the World kind of reminded me of a review of Bright that I watched when it came out. The reviewer was intrigued by one of the lines the Mexican sheriff has in response to something the orc says about orc prejudice. He says something like &quot;yeah Mexicans still get shit for the Alamo&quot;. Which prompted the reviewer to ask, 'were there orcs at the Alamo?' Their point was that if all these fantasy races had existed up until that point in history, why would all major events happen exactly the same?<br /> <br /> And that kind of sums up how I feel about what I've read about The World. Again I'm not saying it's bad I just feel like it creates more questions than it answers. It's my understand the World is very very similar to our world but all myths are real and the populace are aware of this. But wouldn't all this massively change history? They don't seem to mention it but would most of the now major world religions even exist if the religions of the ancient world literally had gods that people knew for certain existed and had even met? I won't go into all the other questions it created in my mind about changes to major world events throughout history. I guess that's the interesting thing. The idea of Demi-gods in the world wars. Satyrs at the Somme. Treants at the Council of Trent. But it just felt to me like trying to write your cake and eat it too. All of this is different but also it's practically the same. <br /> <br /> So yeah, am I reading it wrong? Does any feel the same or differently? I do really like Scion and look forward to running it but I wanted to air my views on this bit and see how others felt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4612-solar-lantern","name":"Solar Lantern","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T13:53:11-07:00","id":1236887,"title":"","content":"I'd point you to an answer that I saw in another thread. Basically, it's not that orcs and trolls and such are an everyday event. I mean, hurricanes happen all the time, but I don't know their inner workings or how and when they'd form. But I know they exist. I also know that when they do show up, it's bad, and I hope one doesn't happen in my hometown. I think the point is that, more or less, the world is the same. Gods and satyrs don't go around interacting with people, they specifically avoid it. However, some learned scholars may teach college courses on them, and how to appease an ogre so it won't eat you, just like a widerness survival course. However, I also think that each &quot;World&quot; is going to be very different based on each storytellers style, so I don't think there's ever going to be a real answer to your question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24418-dracheau","name":"Dracheau","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T14:06:40-07:00","id":1236892,"title":"","content":"Here's an incorrect assumption that seems to be made.<br /> <br /> People often in my experience ask &quot;Why is there still Christianity if the other religions exist?&quot;<br /> <br /> The response to that is why do you assume the Christianities and other Abrahamic-derived religions are wrong? A big thing in The World is that all myths are true.<br /> <br /> All.<br /> <br /> As for &quot;Wait if these gods existed why did things turn out similarly, wouldn't wars have gone differently?&quot; well riddle me this: Why assume that it wasn't a case of both sides invoking magic and curses? Hell, it's Canon that Roman attack on the Gaulish people still happened, and the Gauls called upon their Scions and Gods.<br /> <br /> The thing is, the Romans had the Theoi. And the Roman legions were led by one Iulius Caesar, Scion of Venus.<br /> <br /> It doesn't fit the parallel with Bright because Bright introduces new different things. These legends Scion touches on, the myths and religions of old, have and in many ways still do shape our culture today. In Ireland, they build roads around fairy rings. Disturbing one is something Not Done.<br /> <br /> And this is in out world, where stepping in a Fariy Ring won't actually whisk you away to their realm. In The World, it very well can.<br /> <br /> Saying &quot;Things would have turned out completely different&quot; is insincere in my mind, and neglects to consider how these legends and religions influenced people's actions throughout our own history. The biggest differences between our world and The World is one, the polytheistic religions endured more than they did here, though are not necessarily the dominant ones. And two, the creatures of legend and folklore are real.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T14:31:53-07:00","id":1236899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar Lantern</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1236881-thoughts-on-the-world#post1236881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I finally got around to reading the Origins pdf and I've only just read through the setting and the explanation of The World. I want to see how others feel about it because I'm not sure how I do. I'll also preface all this by saying I'm aware that you can just make up your own setting if you don't like the one in the book and what not. I also don't dislike what I've read so far. But maybe I need to re-read it or get other people's opinions on it. <br /> <br /> Reading through the description of the World kind of reminded me of a review of Bright that I watched when it came out. The reviewer was intrigued by one of the lines the Mexican sheriff has in response to something the orc says about orc prejudice. He says something like &quot;yeah Mexicans still get shit for the Alamo&quot;. Which prompted the reviewer to ask, 'were there orcs at the Alamo?' Their point was that if all these fantasy races had existed up until that point in history, why would all major events happen exactly the same?<br /> <br /> And that kind of sums up how I feel about what I've read about The World. Again I'm not saying it's bad I just feel like it creates more questions than it answers. It's my understand the World is very very similar to our world but all myths are real and the populace are aware of this. But wouldn't all this massively change history? They don't seem to mention it but would most of the now major world religions even exist if the religions of the ancient world literally had gods that people knew for certain existed and had even met? I won't go into all the other questions it created in my mind about changes to major world events throughout history. I guess that's the interesting thing. The idea of Demi-gods in the world wars. Satyrs at the Somme. Treants at the Council of Trent. But it just felt to me like trying to write your cake and eat it too. All of this is different but also it's practically the same. <br /> <br /> So yeah, am I reading it wrong? Does any feel the same or differently? I do really like Scion and look forward to running it but I wanted to air my views on this bit and see how others felt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would gods change the outcome of any given mortal squabble that\u2019s over in the blink of an eye from their perspective? And if they do care, wouldn\u2019t they be fighting other divine beings who care about this super important war? And whose to say they didn\u2019t shape it - look at Jonathan Strange and Mr Norrell\u2019s version of the Napoleonic Wars. Magic plays a crucial role in British victory - the fact that this is a change from our world does not require a change in outcome.<br /> <br /> This is not a setting like Bright where Satyrs and Naga are minority groups in school or work alongside you. They exist on the periphery - most people never knowingly encounter them, but their existence isn\u2019t a secret.<br /> <br /> The problem with Bright is trying to use \u201cdemihumans\u201d as minority allegory while still keeping all the inter-human society aspects the same. That\u2019s not the case here. Most people lived lives exactly like ones they live in our world with no higher presence of nonhumans and the supernatural beyond vague awareness that it\u2019s \u201cout there\u201d.<br /> <br /> In other words the world works EXACTLY like described in mythology.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s why it confuses me that this confuses people. In the primary source material for this game, Ancient peoples believed in the divine and numinous and its existence was a fact of life while most people never encountered it. The fact that there was no conspiracies to hide the numinous did not stop it from being out of sight of most people (hence most ancient Indians believeing in Naga and Rakshasa without meeting one). So why is it so hard for that type of setting to work if people also have cars?<br /> <br /> Also there are not other \u201cmajor\u201d religions - inserting the word \u201cmajor\u201d changes the setting from how it\u2019s written significantly. There are SMALL religions that have continuously existed in the World, that\u2019s only counterparts in our world are reconstructed, not continuous faiths.<br /> <br /> Monotheism doesn\u2019t need to deny there are a bunch of powerful beings on Mt Olympus to say \u201cthere is only one True God deserving of worship.\u201d Atheists don\u2019t need to deny the existence of the Kami as a fact of the natural world to consider them an emergent part of the natural world set in motion by the Big Bang.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 07-19-2018, 11:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T14:56:33-07:00","id":1236909,"title":"","content":"All that said, I do have some note worthy differences in the Word vs reality, thanks to the heroism of past Scions at my own table. One significant example is that thanks to Manitou, Wakanpi, Orenda, Diyin Dine\u2019e, Kachina, etc etc Scions - Native Americans held a much stronger footing against European/US imperialism, and as a result their populations are higher, religious traditions are stronger, and their sovereign lands are larger, controlling more resources, and are less subject to the Federal or State governments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T20:10:07-07:00","id":1236994,"title":"","content":"So, by what I readed in here, Scion 2nd is more to &quot;The Secret World/Secret World: Legends&quot; (the computer MMO game) than to Bright. I mean, the magic/fantasy/myth is there. Maybe not in the spotlight, but there. But also not exactly secret. It's there. If you wanna see it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23841-hayashi","name":"Hayashi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23841_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T20:18:07-07:00","id":1236997,"title":"","content":"Glamour brings up a good point. Like, a lot of our history in this world today, people assumed that many of these beings WERE alive, just kept to themselves. They didn't doubt that naga and fairies existed. To the Greeks, they <i>knew</i> that the Gods lived on a mountain. Not a metaphor for a heavenly realm, but like, a literal mountain. Over thereabouts. *Waves vaguely at the horizon* They <i>knew</i> that if you got a shovel and started digging, eventually you'd breach into the Underworld and into the realm of Hades. Don't do that, dude does NOT take kindly to people just waltzing into his realm.<br /> <br /> Like... Scientific studies say that gods, kitsune, werewolves, that none of those are real.<br /> <br /> But for most of history, they were accepted <i>as</i> real. They were real to those people, even if they weren't there.<br /> <br /> It's just that in Scion's The World... People still accept these things as real. Because they <i>are</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T20:34:42-07:00","id":1237001,"title":"","content":"I see both side to this, but the important difference between the &quot;myths&quot; in our world and the other active faiths of Scion, is that in our world, to give just one example, the Greeks stopped believing in &quot;the Gods on the mountain&quot; as a large part of their daily life, because other faiths [generally, monotheistic ones] overran the old ways. And they did so because, arguably, there weren't any &quot;real&quot; Gods to step in and remind the faithful that they were there. [I'm trying not to get into a theological discussion about our world and faith - I'm talking about the game world here]<br /> I personally feel that Zeus would have taken some steps to ensure that worship of his entire Pantheon wasn't relegated to &quot;ancient mythology&quot; by an upstart faith of <i>any </i>stripe, and that Odin, Horus, Amaterasu, and all of the others out there would have done the same. You don't have to actually manifest to prove the point if you can still send scions, monsters, minions, miracles, and the like to remind people &quot;hey, guys, I'm watching you.&quot; It just seems a bit to pat to me that entire Pantheons of divine beings with a vested interest in keeping humanity alive and kicking would spawn a world that is functionally the same as ours, just with more temples and minor faiths. Egypt during the period when Horus and Hathor were predominant, is a very different place from the current country where Islam dominates everything. I understand that the writers are trying to avoid offending people, and that we can do what we want [and I have certainly done so in my own campaign], but I do think that the &quot;default&quot; world is a bit too &quot;different but the same.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T20:40:54-07:00","id":1237003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hayashi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1236881-thoughts-on-the-world?p=1236994#post1236994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, by what I readed in here, Scion 2nd is more to &amp;quot;The Secret World/Secret World: Legends&amp;quot; (the computer MMO game) than to Bright. I mean, the magic/fantasy/myth is there. Maybe not in the spotlight, but there. But also not exactly secret. It's there. If you wanna see it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t know the thing you\u2019re specifically referencing, but yes that sounds right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T21:26:05-07:00","id":1237015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1236881-thoughts-on-the-world?p=1237001#post1237001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally feel that Zeus would have taken some steps to ensure that worship of his entire Pantheon wasn't relegated to &quot;ancient mythology&quot; by an upstart faith of <i>any </i>stripe, and that Odin, Horus, Amaterasu, and all of the others out there would have done the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mistaken Assumption, and one that goes <i>entirely</i> against the game itself.<br /> <br /> The religions of those gods in the World are emphatically <i>not dead</i>. Like, the worship is still there. There are temples to all those Pantheons, throughout the World.<br /> <br /> Maybe not the majority stranglehold, but they're there, and accepted, to the point where if Religion comes up in the office it's not odd to hear someone say &quot;Yeah made an offering to Hades so hopefully the next quarter looks better, am I right?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T22:28:07-07:00","id":1237030,"title":"","content":"There's also the point that while Scion is a setting where all faith is real, and one largely based off our own world, it's ALSO a world with it's own bits of unifying cosmology. One of those things being Fate, and Fatebinding, and the general decision that Gods mostly eventually turned away from intervening quite so much because they were tired of being carved into new shapes by human beliefs and had enough Mantles already thank you very much. Some Pantheons did this more heavily than others, of course, but it is one of those things that you're supposed to be able to rely upon,-- a pillar of the setting as it were,- to help suspend your suspension of disbelief.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/728-crownedsun","name":"CrownedSun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar728_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"217"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T07:09:24-07:00","id":1237130,"title":"","content":"To Kyman201 - you misunderstand me. I'm saying that, because all of the faiths are real and active, not subsumed by the monotheistic faiths of our real world, the Gods would have had an influence on culture and government that was great enough to make the modern world of Scion a very different place from ours. I realize the Theoi are real and openly worshipped - that was my point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T08:04:44-07:00","id":1237145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1236881-thoughts-on-the-world?p=1237130#post1237130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To Kyman201 - you misunderstand me. I'm saying that, because all of the faiths are real and active, not subsumed by the monotheistic faiths of our real world, the Gods would have had an influence on culture and government that was great enough to make the modern world of Scion a very different place from ours. I realize the Theoi are real and openly worshipped - that was my point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I go back to the Jonathan Strange example. The result of the supernatural playing an active role in history and government does not need to be a different outcome. The Theoi and their worship playing an active role in US society results in Greco-Roman architecture dominating the capital, the embrace of a Seatorial political system by the Founding Father\u2019s, etc etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T08:05:29-07:00","id":1237147,"title":"","content":"Honestly I'd just split the difference and call it a day. Ancient polytheistic religions are <i>slightly</i> more popular in the &quot;World&quot; than our world, Hinduism being the obvious exception, but Islam, Christianity, and Judaism are vastly more popular and most people consider the likes of Zeus and Odin to just be ancient myths like in our world. <br /> <br /> My main problem with the &quot;World&quot; 2e is the idea that people know that ogres and giants exist. Sure, most people will never encounter them but rarity doesn't mean that people wouldn't rightfully be terrified of them eating their families and create entire government agencies and laws to deal with them. If want to keep the setting similar to our world I say make it so that the supernatural is a secret that's slowly being revealed to the world as the Titans become an issue. That way the PCs are signaling the dawn of something wonderous and horrifying coming to the &quot;World&quot; instead of something that has been normalized to a degree.<br /> <br /> I mean, which is cooler. People screaming &quot;That's impossible! Dragons don't exist,&quot; while one suddenly shows up to fight our heroes or &quot;Hey, look guys its another dragon. It's neat to see one up close instead of on a Youtube clip.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T09:30:31-07:00","id":1237175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1236881-thoughts-on-the-world?p=1237147#post1237147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I'd just split the difference and call it a day. Ancient polytheistic religions are <i>slightly</i> more popular in the &quot;World&quot; than our world, Hinduism being the obvious exception, but Islam, Christianity, and Judaism are vastly more popular and most people consider the likes of Zeus and Odin to just be ancient myths like in our world. <br /> <br /> My main problem with the &quot;World&quot; 2e is the idea that people know that ogres and giants exist. Sure, most people will never encounter them but rarity doesn't mean that people wouldn't rightfully be terrified of them eating their families and create entire government agencies and laws to deal with them. If want to keep the setting similar to our world I say make it so that the supernatural is a secret that's slowly being revealed to the world as the Titans become an issue. That way the PCs are signaling the dawn of something wonderous and horrifying coming to the &quot;World&quot; instead of something that has been normalized to a degree.<br /> <br /> I mean, which is cooler. People screaming &quot;That's impossible! Dragons don't exist,&quot; while one suddenly shows up to fight our heroes or &quot;Hey, look guys its another dragon. It's neat to see one up close instead of on a Youtube clip.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Between those two, the latter is definitely cooler. The former requires people be very stupid and somehow be deluded about things that objectively exist not existing. People (mostly) don\u2019t believe in dragons in real life because they don\u2019t exist. If they actually existed, belief in them would never have gone away in the first place.<br /> <br /> That said, seeing a dragon should still be so awe inspiring that people shouldn\u2019t be blas\u00e9 about it - but the denialist cliche is a tired boring trope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T09:40:23-07:00","id":1237179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar Lantern</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1236881-thoughts-on-the-world#post1236881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their point was that if all these fantasy races had existed up until that point in history, why would all major events happen exactly the same?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> If I remember correctly, there was a whole topic in which we debated that very question. If the Gods never chose to abandon the World and continued to interact with us, then it makes sense that The World of Scion would be almost completely unrecognizable from The World that we know of in real life. I'm pretty sure the Aztec pantheon would step in if they noticed the Europeans were massacring their worshipers and destroying their culture.<br /> <br /> And if the genocide of the Aztec empire was either prevented or at the very least severely impeded, then what does that mean for the Europeans who came to colonize their land?<br /> <br /> This scenario is but only one example of the changes to history that would likely take place in a world where the Gods are present and active in our daily lives.<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> As for the idea of the Gods remaining in the periphery, I think that's a poorly thought out argument. Because you're failing to take into account the personalities of these Gods and the culture they derived from.<br /> <br /> Take the Theoi for example, this pantheon was extraordinarily vain and wrathful. If they caught a mortal speaking one unkind word about them, they would go above and beyond the call of duty to wreak godly vengeance upon them. You really think they're just going to sit back on their mountain and wave off changes made to their image and reputation just because the mortals of the world are showing signs of becoming more progressive?<br /> <br /> Having been a big fan of Greek Mythology when I was younger, I can tell you that is certainly not going to be the case!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-20-2018, 12:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T09:58:57-07:00","id":1237183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1236881-thoughts-on-the-world?p=1237175#post1237175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Between those two, the latter is definitely cooler. The former requires people be very stupid and somehow be deluded about things that objectively exist not existing. People (mostly) don\u2019t believe in dragons in real life because they don\u2019t exist. If they actually existed, belief in them would never have gone away in the first place.<br /> <br /> That said, seeing a dragon should still be so awe inspiring that people shouldn\u2019t be blas\u00e9 about it - but the denialist cliche is a tired boring trope.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think there's been a misunderstanding. I don't want people to deny that the supernatural even though there has been blatant obvious of it being around for awhile. I'd just prefer the supernatural to be a thing that's only recently come around again, thus causing people who first encounter it to be disbelief for a time but eventually come to grips with it.<br /> <br /> Basically, like Scion 1e where the setting assumed the Gods, Scions and magic haven't been around for millienia and that the PC's are a sign of a new age of mythmaking and magic. I just think its more interesting for the PCs if normal people don't immediately see the guy throwing lightning everywhere and know their likely a Scion of Thor or Indra whose there to help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T11:11:51-07:00","id":1237204,"title":"","content":"Oh, yeah, a setting where the divine is a recent emergence throwing the world into c haps would make a good setting shard for the future! But I get why it\u2019s not the default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T11:57:54-07:00","id":1237220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1236881-thoughts-on-the-world?p=1237183#post1237183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, like Scion 1e where the setting assumed the Gods, Scions and magic haven't been around for millienia and that the PC's are a sign of a new age of mythmaking and magic. I just think its more interesting for the PCs if normal people don't immediately see the guy throwing lightning everywhere and know their likely a Scion of Thor or Indra whose there to help.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man I dunno what setting you're thinking of, but that wasn't 1e. The 1e assumption was that the magic stuff was always there, it was just in hiding.<br /> <br /> For some reason.<br /> <br /> Like the Gods didn't go to sleep for a thousand years, they remained poking at things throughout history. They just let their religions vanish and people forget they were myths because <i>shut up</i><i> and stop asking questions</i>. There's not even a handwave like wizards going around with memory charms, or some kind of supernatural Mist that keeps mortals from realizing that the divine exists. It's just accepted that there's giants and other Titanspawn (and the books say that these Titanspawn have always existed leaking out through the prison the Titans are in) that Scions have been fighting (basically EVERY historical person of importance has been a Scion in 1e)<br /> <br /> And yet NO mortal has realized that these people flinging about divine miracles and fighting these monsters exist. For some reason. Why not? How? Your power stat in Scion is your Legend, the imprint of how famous you are, but nobody realizes you're divine?<br /> <br /> Frankly, the major difference in the settings between the editions is that the 2e mortals aren't idiots.<br /> <br /> And I honestly find your comment of someone seeing a dragon just going &quot;oh neat a dragon huh&quot; to be disingenuous. Like, okay. Elephants. You know they exist. You may have even seen one in a zoo.<br /> <br /> But if an elephant suddenly was walking down the street where you live, your reaction would, I'd bet real money, <b>not</b> be &quot;Oh huh, an elephant, cool&quot;. It'd be &quot;Wait WHAT? Holy crap THAT'S AN ELEPHANT! I need to get a picture I've never seen one this close before!&quot;<br /> <br /> And that's for a <i>real animal</i> that <i>really exists</i>.<br /> <br /> I admit I may find the &quot;Well if people know about it the magic vanishes and it's all mundane&quot; to be an inherently pessimistic mindset.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T12:36:29-07:00","id":1237230,"title":"","content":"But I never made such a pessimistic assumption. I just stated that people might be more excited to know that supernatural exists after thinking that didn't it, as opposed to people who know it does but only see it rarely. I'm not saving they'd be totally blase about it, just that I personally thought the world slowly learning about the existence of the supernatural could be a more interesting setting hook that made the actions and exploits of the PCs more unique and unexpected. Of course, I could see other people thinking differently and finding such a premise oldhat.<br /> <br /> My point was that if Scion 2e is going to go the Gods, monsters and magic exists and have been around that everyone knows about it but the world is still more or less the same route, I'd kind of want them to go a bit further with the alternate history or at the very least make mentions to how the World has adapted to dragons being a thing that people have to worry about. Maybe there's government branch that deals with Fire-Breathing Megafauna or maybe there are research facilities that try to scientifically explain how magic works in relation to physics. Sort of like how Hunter: The Vigil has various organizations that deal with the fact that supernatural predators and forces exists, but without WOD's assumption that the supernatural and these organizations are a secret.<br /> <br /> Now, of course, Scions aka the PCs are the ones who are supposed to fill the spot of protagonists that go out there and fight the monsters, but I hope that 2e doesn't ignore that there would, and should, be important mortal organizations not necessarily related to the Gods that are involved with managing the existence of the supernatural. Maybe cops in the World are trained to use sorcrey to deal with supernatural criminals. Or hell, maybe sorcery is just taught in schools along with science and mathematics. Perhaps that's already been established in a Kickstarter post I missed, or maybe Scion Companion will have something similar to what I'm taking about. In any case, I just hope that the gameline fleshes out and expands how the World has responded and deviated from our own in interesting ways.<br /> <br /> Lastly, I will fully admit that I'm working on my memories of Scion 1e books and admit that your probably write about the magic thing. My table house-ruled that game so much that its more than likely that some aspects of the setting were just tossed out and forgotten resulting in my skewered recollection of things. Thank you for setting me straight if that is the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1675,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","user":"Weirdboyz","date":". 07-20-2018, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T13:04:46-07:00","id":1237234,"title":"","content":"I admit i\u2019m Just so god damn tired of \u201cthe supernatural is hiding... because!\u201d trope - combined with \u201cpeople cling to rationality and refuse to believe in miracles\u201d and other bullshit that isn\u2019t remotely true about human nature being the default of urban fantasy - it is seriously refreshing to see a setting not do that.<br /> <br /> Now, as I said, I\u2019m ALSO open to a \u201cthe divine has been gone, but now it\u2019s returning and this will cause major changes as the world reacts\u201d setting! That would be seriously cool as well - but in the mean time the World works better as the first introduced default setting.<br /> <br /> <br /> The 2E material does refer to special government and military, etc reactions to the supernatural, so those differences are there, just not focused on because mortals suck at dealing with the supernatural compared to Scions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 07-20-2018, 04:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T13:16:53-07:00","id":1237237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1236881-thoughts-on-the-world?p=1237234#post1237234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The 2E material does refer to special government and military, etc reactions to the supernatural, so those differences are there, just not focused on because mortals suck at dealing with the supernatural compared to Scions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that's good to know. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T13:42:15-07:00","id":1237251,"title":"","content":"Here, there's a sidebar in the Hero outline, let me just quote it...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Heroic Expectations<br /> Beneath silent respect, fawning worship, and fear, mortals hold Heroes to an implied duty: <u>Protect us, and act as our representative among divine and legendary powers.</u> Heroes bind, tame, or slay monsters. They plead the people\u2019s case before angry Gods, or tell mortals what the Gods want. They explain why children vanish on the full moon by the ancient mounds, and if they can\u2019t convince the beings inside to give the kids back, they can at least tell mortals how to prevent it from happening again. Sometimes holy covenants spell these expectations out, but most of the time people expect Heroes to do it because of who they are.<br /> <br /> When Heroes skip town when monsters come around or shrug when cultists ask them why Zeus is getting generous with his thunderbolts, mortals take note. Leaving aside the consequences to a Hero\u2019s Legend, shirking these ancient duties damages their reputation in mortal society. The cult doesn\u2019t invite them to rituals. People in the mythic underground snicker or shake their heads in conversations just out of the Hero\u2019s presumed earshot. The Gods have a way of finding out, too, and might explicitly discipline a reluctant Hero, but fear usually limits mortal reactions to quiet contempt and shunning, save for acidic comments in social media, where mortals exhibit more bravery.<br /> <br /> Storyguides should warn socially adept Heroes about the consequences of avoiding mythic dangers, and leave it to them to respond. If they still don\u2019t want to bother with monsters and strange gates, well, mortal disdain shouldn\u2019t be a punishment, but an impetus for a new story. </div> </div> </div>Like, being a Hero should be a BIG thing for a Scion. Even if people KNOW that Indra and Zeus have champions, that won't necessarily make it any less miraculous when you see a giant in the street, and while the cops are getting civilians out of there you see a lone figure step forward and draw a sword that crackles with lightning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T15:28:10-07:00","id":1237307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1236881-thoughts-on-the-world?p=1237183#post1237183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think there's been a misunderstanding. I don't want people to deny that the supernatural even though there has been blatant obvious of it being around for awhile. I'd just prefer the supernatural to be a thing that's only recently come around again, thus causing people who first encounter it to be disbelief for a time but eventually come to grips with it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Actually, that was the premise for Scion 1E.<br /> <br /> Titans were sealed away, and the Gods chose to remain absent from mortal life, thus causing them to fade into myth. Then the Titans broke free, and the Gods started getting more involved again.<br /> <br /> But the setting of 2E is apparently that the Gods never left, and not all of the Titans were considered deserving of imprisonment. They've stuck around all these centuries, so public awareness of their existence should be common knowledge. As should the consequences that are expected to come with their presence in the mortal World.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1236881-thoughts-on-the-world?p=1237234#post1237234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit i\u2019m Just so god damn tired of \u201cthe supernatural is hiding... because!\u201d trope - combined with \u201cpeople cling to rationality and refuse to believe in miracles\u201d and other bullshit that isn\u2019t remotely true about human nature being the default of urban fantasy - it is seriously refreshing to see a setting not do that.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Completely agree with this! I don't mind the supernatural going into hiding in regards to World of Darkness, because they have a legitimate reason for doing so in the sense they were almost destroyed by a human uprising. But in the world of Scion, they make it very clear that mortals wouldn't stand a snowball's chance in Hell against the kind of threats that lurk out there.<br /> <br /> <br /> I once heard from somebody who's name I don't remember anymore that <i>&quot;A skeptic does not deny the existence of the supernatural. A skeptic demands evidence of the supernatural.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Well, correct me if I'm wrong, but I think if a highschool student rolled up in my neighborhood on a flying car and whipped out a pistol that fired bolts of lightning before entering battle with a 10 foot ice man, I'd be pretty fucking convinced that the Norse may have been on to something!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-20-2018, 06:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T15:31:35-07:00","id":1237309,"title":"","content":"You can certainly play it any way you want, but for me, it seems that taking the premise of Scion - the Gods are real and take a role in things, their offspring do heroic and legendary stuff, magic is more than trucks, and mythical beings are out there to be found - and still saying &quot;but the world is basically the same anyway&quot;, is unsatisfying from a creative perspective. You can do it if you want, or if you don't have time or inclination to change things, but I definitely prefer to shake things up. YMMV, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T16:18:57-07:00","id":1237330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1236881-thoughts-on-the-world?p=1237309#post1237309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can certainly play it any way you want, but for me, it seems that taking the premise of Scion - the Gods are real and take a role in things, their offspring do heroic and legendary stuff, magic is more than trucks, and mythical beings are out there to be found - and still saying &quot;but the world is basically the same anyway&quot;, is unsatisfying from a creative perspective. You can do it if you want, or if you don't have time or inclination to change things, but I definitely prefer to shake things up. YMMV, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div> Here\u2019s what i don\u2019t get - I don\u2019t think anyone would suggest a setting based on mythic Greece, that presented the lives and politics of Ancient Greece accurately, but has the supernatural they believed in existing parallel, and epic heroes running around, was somehow a contradiction. So why is it a problem if that exact same concept is applied to the modern world setting instead?<br /> <br /> I go back to Jonathan Strange and Mr Norrell of my touchstone of the Union of mundane and supernatural, and how changing history to incorporate the supernatural does not necessitate a change in outcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 07-20-2018, 07:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T17:08:08-07:00","id":1237342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1236881-thoughts-on-the-world?p=1237330#post1237330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here\u2019s what\u2019s i don\u2019t get - I don\u2019t think anyone would suggest a setting based on mythic Greece, that presented the lives and politics of Ancient Greece accurately, but has the supernatural they believed in existing parallel, and epic heroes running around, was somehow a contradiction. So why is it a problem if that exact same concept is applied to the modern world setting instead?<br /> <br /> I go back to Jonathan Strange and Mr Norrell of my touchstone of the Union of mundane and supernatural, and how changing history to incorporate the supernatural does not necessitate a change in outcome.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> While I'm willing to believe that mythical creatures might dwell on the fringes of human civilization (as mythology seems to suggest), you are once again forgetting to account for the personalities and cultures that surround the various pantheons.<br /> <br /> <br /> Take the Devas, for example. I'm not Hindu and don't claim to have any in depth knowledge about their beliefs, but I've heard some accounts regarding how their pantheon has access to its own arsenal of WMD's they can launch at their enemies if they start becoming a problem. How do you think a foreign power is going to oppose the Hindu people when their gods have access to nukes thousands of years before any other country even knows that nukes are possible?<br /> <br /> <br /> And then there's the concept of various War Gods and their followers. Oh, good idea, let's wage war against an army that worships the act of war!<br /> <br /> <br /> These and any other instance in which mortals have attempted to forcefully convert people in large numbers would play out much differently if the Gods were present and accounted for. They are not going to just sit back and watch as their faiths are demonized, their people massacred and their very way of life being irreperably changed by hostile forces and other radical groups.<br /> <br /> If things start getting out of hand, they are going to step in and take action. And I think we can all agree that people attributed with the creation of the cosmos are infinitely more likely to win a fight than people swinging around sharpened pieces of metal, and who only discovered gun powder by complete accident!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T17:24:11-07:00","id":1237345,"title":"","content":"Ancient peoples waged war on each other all the time while believing in gods including those who may favor their enemies. Why would that be different in the modern world?<br /> <br /> Why are you assuming gods would take notice of such wars beyond expecting heroism on the part of their Scions?<br /> <br /> The Astras are not used against mortal targets. The Earth would be hard pressed to survive it, since all the damage an astra deals must actually be dealt - any in excess of killing the target radiates out from the liquified target destroying until all the damage is dealt.<br /> <br /> Using one against anything less than a full god-level Asura would be monstrously reckless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T20:48:14-07:00","id":1237390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1236881-thoughts-on-the-world?p=1237309#post1237309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can certainly play it any way you want, but for me, it seems that taking the premise of Scion - the Gods are real and take a role in things, their offspring do heroic and legendary stuff, magic is more than trucks, and mythical beings are out there to be found - and still saying &quot;but the world is basically the same anyway&quot;, is unsatisfying from a creative perspective. You can do it if you want, or if you don't have time or inclination to change things, but I definitely prefer to shake things up. YMMV, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not a critique, just genuine curiosity. What would be a radical change that you would see the continuous presence of divine entity cause? Would you go as far as the Americas never formed and instead there is a ... League of First Nations in the new continent, for example???","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T21:19:17-07:00","id":1237401,"title":"","content":"Honestly? I would go back to around the year 1 CE, and work out from there. What happens when Christianity starts? Does it get a foothold? Is Jesus a Scion or just a politician? How do the Alihah and Annunaki and Yazatas react when Islam targets their shrines? Does Odin allow Christians (if they ever become relevant) to convert the Norse? How does Communism come from a land watched over by the Bogovi? And yes, what happens to the European settlement of North America? Does it get a foothold? Do the native Gods prevent diseases and foreign invaders from wiping out their chosen people? Do women have more rights in cultures with strong, active Goddesses? Would slavery have gone the way it did, with no America to feed it? (I simplify issues for illustrative purposes - please don't take this to mean I trivialize or point fingers where sensitive topics are concerned)<br /> I would be prepared to rewrite history, because I don't think it would go the way it did if the Gods of all cultures were real. There would be wars, invasions, border exchanges, and so on, because humans are humans, and War Gods are persuasive, but the world wouldn't be what it is today. And I would set this all out before starting a game, because that's how I GM. Not saying that my way is better or the only right way - just that it's my way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T22:50:36-07:00","id":1237417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1236881-thoughts-on-the-world?p=1237345#post1237345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ancient peoples waged war on each other all the time while believing in gods including those who may favor their enemies. Why would that be different in the modern world?<br /> <br /> Why are you assuming gods would take notice of such wars beyond expecting heroism on the part of their Scions?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm assuming based on individual cases in accordance with how mythology viewed the behavior of such figures. Real world mythology likes to paint the Theoi as overreacting to every slight ever made against them, and they were extremely sore losers. While there have been cases in which the pantheon is depicted as losing a competition that they are supposed to be the pinnacle of excellence at, these stories always resulted in the God throwing a tantrum and the one responsible for beating them suffers a fate worse than death!<br /> <br /> <br /> And as for the Aztecs, if the &quot;All Myths Are True&quot; aspect is what we're going with, then they're telling the truth in that they NEED human sacrifices in order to stop the world from ending. How are they going to do that if the Europeans show up on the Aztec's doorstep and start conducting mass genocide on their entire culture, while forcing the survivors to convert to Christianity? If nobody's performing sacrifices anymore, then that means the Aztec apocalypse is upon us!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And then we have the Loa, who's mythology, as I understand it, blatantly claims that Gods are constantly interacting with mortals on an almost daily basis. Heck, they even possess people's bodies and take them out on joy rides!<br /> <br /> <br /> History in the real world turned out the way that it did because we know better now. There were no gods to answer our prayers and aid us when the enemy was kicking down the gates. But in the world of Scion, the Gods are very much real, they are very much paying attention, and they will very much take exception to seeing the cultural systems they spent thousands of years influencing being wiped out by interference from foreign powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T06:33:11-07:00","id":1237474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1236881-thoughts-on-the-world?p=1237417#post1237417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">History in the real world turned out the way that it did because we know better now. There were no gods to answer our prayers and aid us when the enemy was kicking down the gates. But in the world of Scion, the Gods are very much real, they are very much paying attention, and they will very much take exception to seeing the cultural systems they spent thousands of years influencing being wiped out by interference from foreign powers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And in Scion, the Gods are still fallible and likely backed a lot of the conquests themselves, and answered the prayers of their respective people when they prayed for victory in the invasion. It's also a trait of the World that the Gods don't get along, especially when the mortals Fatebind them into not being on the same side.<br /> <br /> That also ties into how the Theoi are; they can throw tantrums, but when it comes down to it if Zeus starts getting pissy about a Japanese skyscraper, he's going to have to go through Susanoo first to vent his displeasure. This is the same pantheon that holds hospitality as the highest of all virtues, so if it's unintentional? Their people are their guests, so they may rage, but it wasn't a deliberate hubristic act of spite, so to actually respond would be worse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T06:33:11-07:00","id":1237475,"title":"","content":"double post","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T06:59:39-07:00","id":1237485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1236881-thoughts-on-the-world?p=1237474#post1237474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And in Scion, the Gods are still fallible and likely backed a lot of the conquests themselves, and answered the prayers of their respective people when they prayed for victory in the invasion. It's also a trait of the World that the Gods don't get along, especially when the mortals Fatebind them into not being on the same side.<br /> <br /> That also ties into how the Theoi are; they can throw tantrums, but when it comes down to it if Zeus starts getting pissy about a Japanese skyscraper, he's going to have to go through Susanoo first to vent his displeasure. This is the same pantheon that holds hospitality as the highest of all virtues, so if it's unintentional? Their people are their guests, so they may rage, but it wasn't a deliberate hubristic act of spite, so to actually respond would be worse.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> 1 - I thought the manner in which Fatebinds worked is getting a revamp in 2E? I don't fully remember the details, but mortals apparently have less of an impact in shaping the Gods than they did in 1E?<br /> <br /> 2 - You really think the Theoi care if it was intentional or not? *motions towards Hera's general direction*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T08:44:18-07:00","id":1237512,"title":"","content":"I look at it through a distinction between History and Mythology. <br /> <br /> Gods care about Purviews, Virtues and Fatebinding. At what point is direct intervention for the sake of Purviews or Virtues worth the risk of Fatebinding? <br /> <br /> The answer is never. Myths already exist to tell mortals <i>how</i> they should act and <i>why, </i>and the supernatural has enough presence in The World to remind mortals that they should respect the Gods even if they don't affect their daily lives. Slavery still happens, wars still happen, epidemics still happen, technology still happens, because that is the course of History, which is the domain of mortals, not Gods, except its trappings are superimposed with a layer of Mythology because of the Gods' influence.<br /> <br /> Like, Ireland still fought during World War I, but instead of looking like <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ireland_and_World_War_I#/media/File:Irish_WWI_poster_-_Is_Your_Home_Worth_Fighting_For%3F_-_Hely%27s_Limited,_Litho,_Dublin.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>, the recruitment posters looked like <a href=\"https://dumielauxepices.net/sites/default/files/drawn-crow-creepy-526188-5546102.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>, because when the Morrigan wants dead bodies, she's getting dead bodies one way or the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T10:23:22-07:00","id":1237532,"title":"","content":"All of this also begs the question of, like, WHICH god are we talking about?<br /> <br /> Like, okay, Zeus is pissed,-- which Zeus, from which myth, exactly? Maybe it's Jupiter. Maybe it's the Mycenaen Zeus, that wasn't even the head of his Pantheon, and about whom we really don't know all that much honestly. <i>Each of these Zeus are real and true and a thing.</i><br /> <br /> Or... the same thing for every other God.. in probably more complexity than we can easily understand.<br /> <br /> Everything we know about God-level play, at the moment, is that it is VERY VERY DIFFERENT from Hero-level play. It's NOT just, &quot;You have legend 12 and more tools, but otherwise, everything is more or less the same as you're doing right now but BIGGER.&quot; The experience of being a God was, in point of fact, described as being closer to Imperial Mysteries from Mage. It's a more numinous sort of thing. As I said earlier, God's don't mess around THAT directly in mortal affairs because if they do they get fatebound to the point of no longer being themselves. It's death of a different sort.<br /> <br /> (n' yes, Fatebinding functions differently in 2e. It's not actually, like, less of a thing though. It just works in ways that, as a gamer, are better for the game and more fun. n' it DOES get worse as you go up in tier until Gods get fatebound to entire cultures.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/728-crownedsun","name":"CrownedSun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar728_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"217"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T13:56:15-07:00","id":1237578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1236881-thoughts-on-the-world?p=1237417#post1237417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> History in the real world turned out the way that it did because we know better now. There were no gods to answer our prayers and aid us when the enemy was kicking down the gates. But in the world of Scion, the Gods are very much real, they are very much paying attention, and they will very much take exception to seeing the cultural systems they spent thousands of years influencing being wiped out by interference from foreign powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, I find the way you phrase that to be a bit dismissive (if not insulting) towards people who have believed in God(s), both past and present. Saying \u201cwe know better now\u201d implies that we have systematically disproven any form of the Divine, and there are a lot of religious people in the world today that would be offended at that suggestion (at least in relation to their own religion).<br /> Back to the topic at hand: Consider Sarpedon in the Iliad. He was a son of Zeus fated to die in battle. Zeus considered stepping in and saving his life anyway. He is convinced not to on the grounds that the other Gods might do the same for their favored children. That was during a \u201cfamily squabble\u201d. How much more care would be needed when there is potentially apocalyptic warfare at risk? If your kid and the neighbor kid are having a fist fight in the street, how much good is it going to do either of them (or the neighborhood) if you and the other kid\u2019s parent come out and whip out machine guns, or flamethrowers, or rocket launchers? <br /> So, how did the Gods influence history then?<br /> Loki: \u201cHey guys, there\u2019s a bunch of Christians coming, and when they say convert or die, they\u2019re serious. I don\u2019t like them. No, no, put your swords down. I have a better idea. Pretend to convert. Then you can keep doing things properly when they\u2019re not looking, and laugh at them behind their backs.\u201d<br /> When the Library of Alexandria burned, Scions and trusted worshipers were already transporting the most important and sacred texts to a secret and secure location.<br /> That\u2019s the sort of thing that differed. When a bunch of people started screaming for the slaughter of those who wouldn\u2019t convert, the Gods didn\u2019t gear up and head out to crush the foolish mortals and silently hope that their enemies didn\u2019t also have divine protection. No, they helped their most critical people escape, along with sacred objects or teachings. Rather than starting massive god wars that would destroy much of humanity and leave the World a wasteland, they let the mortals fight their own battles with Scions as their protectors. They didn\u2019t worry about whether their people were dominant, only that they would survive to birth the next generation and pass down their important teachings. The fact that the World has noticeable populations of people that passed down the old religions in an unbroken line isn\u2019t a tiny change. It\u2019s fucking huge! <br /> So why do we still have large populations of monotheistic religions? Because people are people. It only takes the right argument to convince someone. \u201cIf your Gods are so mighty, why haven\u2019t they stopped me from doing this to you? Clearly it\u2019s because they fear the might of my God, which is far greater than they could ever hope to match!\u201d \u201cSure, your \u2018god\u2019 is real, but they\u2019re not really a God. Mine is, and if you don\u2019t convert, well, I\u2019m sure you\u2019ll have plenty of company in the eternal fiery tortures that await you in Hell.\u201d Monotheism also has the benefit of exclusivity. The followers of Dionysus don\u2019t care if you go to Christmas mass with your family. What would the church group think of your plan to attend a ritual celebration for Dionysus, though? When you only honor one God, it cuts off potential worship from others.<br /> Wow, I\u2019m really rambling on at this point. I\u2019m going to stop myself here for now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T14:10:11-07:00","id":1237580,"title":"","content":"And again, why the assumption that in The World, the various Christian sects are less right than the other religions?<br /> <br /> Like, there's no reason to doubt it. All myths are true.<br /> <br /> All of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T14:17:19-07:00","id":1237583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1236881-thoughts-on-the-world?p=1237417#post1237417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">History in the real world turned out the way that it did because we know better now. There were no gods to answer our prayers and aid us when the enemy was kicking down the gates. But in the world of Scion, the Gods are very much real, they are very much paying attention, and they will very much take exception to seeing the cultural systems they spent thousands of years influencing being wiped out by interference from foreign powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every single Pantheon in Scion has worshipers in our World... some of them may be unbroken traditions, some of them may be wildly different from ancient times and some of them may be wholly reconstructed, but they are the spiritual core for an innumerable number of people, and I wold appreciate it if you didn't dismiss all these people as delusional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T19:03:44-07:00","id":1237646,"title":"","content":"<i>You never stop to think about those footnotes in the news. &quot;A local girl was attacked by a demon wolf. Authorities have assured that a child of Thor is seeking it out. The girl is recovering in a hospital.&quot; This is something that sort of gets thrown in at the end of the broadcast and you pay enough attention to realize it was in a different neighborhood far away from your part of the millions of people in this city. Then you forget about it and go on with your daily life.<br /> <br /> If it's something bigger, like an active monster rampage or zombie uprising? That'll get more details and calls for caution in the affected areas. You'll cover your mouth and gasp or cross your arms and frown. You'll talk about &quot;those poor people&quot; or &quot;who let this happen?&quot; or something else. If it is something pleasant or good, like a kitsune marriage or a blessing from a djinn, you might feel a little jealous. But then the event ends and in a week or two it becomes a faded memory for you. Like the tornado that didn't hit your town or the war in foreign lands that you're not fighting. You just tend not to think about it.<br /> <br /> At least until you're part of the footnote. I mean, if you're that college student that took a wrong turn into a satyr kegger, or that actress that got cursed when her agent toyed with Egyptian sorcery, or that girl who survived an attack by a demon wolf. If you're that person. Then everything's changed.<br /> <br /> We always forget that it's not a footnote to that person until we are that person.</i><br /> <br /> -------------------------------<br /> Yeah, I like the fringes thing. I'd venture to say that the supernatural population of the world is probably in the six digits which a lot less than 1%. Dispersion would keep them outliers rather than full on minorities. There would be Terra Incognita where people have day-to-day lives with satyr post-men and angelic police officers (for a mixed pantheon incognita) and a few overworld shards, and these might very well have large populations of their own, but they're not going to be interacting with Earth usually.<br /> <br /> On Earth, one college campus somewhere might have a collection of satyr descended denizens that goes off and parties in a tiny terra incognita somewhere, but I'd be surprised if there were more than three such things so a mortal stumbling on to it would have to be pretty dang unlucky (or lucky depending).<br /> <br /> Very different from Bright.<br /> <br /> In The World, you can talk about your great-great-grandmother, the dryad, and most people would be like &quot;oh, interesting trivia about you.&quot; and then maybe forget it. It's like me saying &quot;I descend from one of the guys who signed the Declaration and Constitution.&quot; There are millions of people who can say the same thing and it's not like they personally had any part of that event so it doesn't really say anything about them. (Though, admittedly, a dryad might still be around to talk to).<br /> <br /> Or for a better example.<br /> <br /> I can say &quot;I live in Japan&quot; where there are currently millions of other people living, including quite a few foreigners like myself. I exist. People who live in Japan exist. But I imagine the majority of Americans or Englishmen or South Africans or so don't think about that most days. Most of the time Japan, or a lot of other foreign countries and even distant cities in your own country, enjoy at best a sort of &quot;I know exists&quot; sort of place in a person's thoughts. And &quot;people who live in Japan&quot; is population size that is higher than The World's population of supernaturals by several orders of magnitude.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T19:43:34-07:00","id":1237662,"title":"","content":"We aren't talking about our world - we're talking about the world of the game. And in that world, real, tangible Gods have real, tangible Scions and other agents to do things. And I think it hubris to presume that the world would still look essentially the same if this were the case. Regardless of your actual beliefs, can we at least agree that religions in our world don't have the same level of provable, observable divine interaction/intervention as in the game? And in the game, the actions of said deities and their agents would have altered the tide of history, IMO, to something quite different. Whether they want to directly interact, or simply play chess, it would lead to a different world. At the very least, because it's more fun to play that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T19:56:52-07:00","id":1237671,"title":"","content":"Taken from a design perspective.<br /> <br /> It makes the most sense to assume divine cancels out divine resulting in basically the same history but with certain legends actually being real supernatural events. Like say the Beast of Gevauden really being a spawn of Fenris or something similar.<br /> <br /> Because this creates the easiest platform for people to mod off of.<br /> <br /> If you take the default setting too far into Alternate History territory then you make it a bit less accessible.<br /> <br /> Most urban fantasies follow the same conceit that, despite the presence of real supernatural things, that history mostly went the way the real world history went.<br /> <br /> Dresden Files, Supernatural, Harry Potter, Young Wizards, Buffy/Angel, etc...they mostly don't toy with history and just focus on the supernatural elements.<br /> <br /> If you want to toy with alternate histories, go for it. But it's not the ideal for the default setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T21:28:25-07:00","id":1237681,"title":"","content":"To the people asking for a wildly different history of the World; why the binary? Why \u201cmust\u201d divine influence change either everything so that the World is nothing like the world we know? \u201cObviously it must be so\u201d goes the argument, but people showed how it isn\u2019t. What\u2019s the logic behind, other than wanting to play a High Fantasy setting in a game geared for Urban Fantasy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T21:49:16-07:00","id":1237687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1236881-thoughts-on-the-world?p=1237578#post1237578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Back to the topic at hand: Consider Sarpedon in the Iliad. He was a son of Zeus fated to die in battle. Zeus considered stepping in and saving his life anyway. He is convinced not to on the grounds that the other Gods might do the same for their favored children. That was during a \u201cfamily squabble\u201d. How much more care would be needed when there is potentially apocalyptic warfare at risk? If your kid and the neighbor kid are having a fist fight in the street, how much good is it going to do either of them (or the neighborhood) if you and the other kid\u2019s parent come out and whip out machine guns, or flamethrowers, or rocket launchers?<br /> So, how did the Gods influence history then?<br /> Loki: \u201cHey guys, there\u2019s a bunch of Christians coming, and when they say convert or die, they\u2019re serious. I don\u2019t like them. No, no, put your swords down. I have a better idea. Pretend to convert. Then you can keep doing things properly when they\u2019re not looking, and laugh at them behind their backs.\u201d<br /> When the Library of Alexandria burned, Scions and trusted worshipers were already transporting the most important and sacred texts to a secret and secure location.<br /> That\u2019s the sort of thing that differed. When a bunch of people started screaming for the slaughter of those who wouldn\u2019t convert, the Gods didn\u2019t gear up and head out to crush the foolish mortals and silently hope that their enemies didn\u2019t also have divine protection. No, they helped their most critical people escape, along with sacred objects or teachings. Rather than starting massive god wars that would destroy much of humanity and leave the World a wasteland, they let the mortals fight their own battles with Scions as their protectors. They didn\u2019t worry about whether their people were dominant, only that they would survive to birth the next generation and pass down their important teachings. The fact that the World has noticeable populations of people that passed down the old religions in an unbroken line isn\u2019t a tiny change. It\u2019s fucking huge!<br /> So why do we still have large populations of monotheistic religions? Because people are people. It only takes the right argument to convince someone. \u201cIf your Gods are so mighty, why haven\u2019t they stopped me from doing this to you? Clearly it\u2019s because they fear the might of my God, which is far greater than they could ever hope to match!\u201d \u201cSure, your \u2018god\u2019 is real, but they\u2019re not really a God. Mine is, and if you don\u2019t convert, well, I\u2019m sure you\u2019ll have plenty of company in the eternal fiery tortures that await you in Hell.\u201d Monotheism also has the benefit of exclusivity. The followers of Dionysus don\u2019t care if you go to Christmas mass with your family. What would the church group think of your plan to attend a ritual celebration for Dionysus, though? When you only honor one God, it cuts off potential worship from others.<br /> Wow, I\u2019m really rambling on at this point. I\u2019m going to stop myself here for now.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Who cares if the world was made into a wasteland? These aren't mortals who have to face the consequences of their reckless behavior for generations to come. These are deities who have the ability to touch a barren patch of dirt with their finger tip and instantly grow a forest that spans for miles around. Disease and pollutants are banished with a mere gesture, and even the iron grip of death itself can be challenged if a God chooses to intervene.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Gods created the universe before, and they can do so again. In fact, quite an awful lot of apocalypse mythos foretells that not only will the world be destroyed, but it will also be reborn in some fashion or another. Hell, the Aztecs have rebuilt the world several times already.<br /> <br /> <br /> And if you think that the gods wouldn't get directly involved in mortal affairs, the Abrahamic faiths would hotly disagree with you. There are stories in which YHVH obliterates entire cities because he found their behavior offensive. Sometimes he would send a Scion to do so, like with the story of Sampson, and other times, he'd send down something much more grandiose, like an Arch Angel!<br /> <br /> This guy was shamelessly flashing his power around in people's faces to prove he was the bestest, most powerful God there ever was. And some say he was even responsible for the Black Death that killed a massive chunk of Europe's population!<br /> <br /> You're telling me the other pantheons aren't going to step in and put a stop to that kind of shit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T22:06:02-07:00","id":1237689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thrythlind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1236881-thoughts-on-the-world?p=1237646#post1237646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[I]<br /> <br /> -------------------------------<br /> Yeah, I like the fringes thing. I'd venture to say that the supernatural population of the world is probably in the six digits which a lot less than 1%. Dispersion would keep them outliers rather than full on minorities. There would be Terra Incognita where people have day-to-day lives with satyr post-men and angelic police officers (for a mixed pantheon incognita) and a few overworld shards, and these might very well have large populations of their own, but they're not going to be interacting with Earth usually.<br /> <br /> On Earth, one college campus somewhere might have a collection of satyr descended denizens that goes off and parties in a tiny terra incognita somewhere, but I'd be surprised if there were more than three such things so a mortal stumbling on to it would have to be pretty dang unlucky (or lucky depending).<br /> <br /> Very different from Bright.<br /> <br /> In The World, you can talk about your great-great-grandmother, the dryad, and most people would be like &quot;oh, interesting trivia about you.&quot; and then maybe forget it. It's like me saying &quot;I descend from one of the guys who signed the Declaration and Constitution.&quot; There are millions of people who can say the same thing and it's not like they personally had any part of that event so it doesn't really say anything about them. (Though, admittedly, a dryad might still be around to talk to).<br /> <br /> Or for a better example.<br /> <br /> I can say &quot;I live in Japan&quot; where there are currently millions of other people living, including quite a few foreigners like myself. I exist. People who live in Japan exist. But I imagine the majority of Americans or Englishmen or South Africans or so don't think about that most days. Most of the time Japan, or a lot of other foreign countries and even distant cities in your own country, enjoy at best a sort of &quot;I know exists&quot; sort of place in a person's thoughts. And &quot;people who live in Japan&quot; is population size that is higher than The World's population of supernaturals by several orders of magnitude.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree with the idea of them choosing to live on the fringes of society, but as for them being minority groups, that seems to be stretching it a bit. <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Some of these pantheons have a population that rivals the global population of earth.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> According to Shintoism, EVERYTHING has a spirit. Including that chair you're sitting in right now, and the computer you're using to read this post. Try to imagine living in the world of <i>The Brave Little Toaster</i>, and you've got a simplified example of the concept.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Celestial Beaurocracy is apparently large enough to have organized themselves into a structured form of government. While the Devas of India number in the millions.<br /> <br /> The reason why they aren't seen in everyday life is because they're usually attributed to residing in another plane of existence, such as the Realm of the Faeries, or whatever else you want to use as an example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T22:42:16-07:00","id":1237693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1236881-thoughts-on-the-world?p=1237687#post1237687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Who cares if the world was made into a wasteland? These aren't mortals who have to face the consequences of their reckless behavior for generations to come. These are deities who have the ability to touch a barren patch of dirt with their finger tip and instantly grow a forest that spans for miles around. Disease and pollutants are banished with a mere gesture, and even the iron grip of death itself can be challenged if a God chooses to intervene.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Gods created the universe before, and they can do so again. In fact, quite an awful lot of apocalypse mythos foretells that not only will the world be destroyed, but it will also be reborn in some fashion or another. Hell, the Aztecs have rebuilt the world several times already.<br /> <br /> <br /> And if you think that the gods wouldn't get directly involved in mortal affairs, the Abrahamic faiths would hotly disagree with you. There are stories in which YHVH obliterates entire cities because he found their behavior offensive. Sometimes he would send a Scion to do so, like with the story of Sampson, and other times, he'd send down something much more grandiose, like an Arch Angel!<br /> <br /> This guy was shamelessly flashing his power around in people's faces to prove he was the bestest, most powerful God there ever was. And some say he was even responsible for the Black Death that killed a massive chunk of Europe's population!<br /> <br /> You're telling me the other pantheons aren't going to step in and put a stop to that kind of shit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe they did. Maybe the reason that archangels aren\u2019t coming down to obliterate entire cities today is that the other pantheons said, \u201cDude, knock it off, or we\u2019re going to get involved in your affairs. You won\u2019t like that.\u201d Hell, maybe that\u2019s the reason that New Testament God seems a bit nicer than Old Testament God.<br /> As for apocalyptic warfare, sure, the Gods could rebuild. But they\u2019re also bound by Fate. The World might need to end in a certain way to be rebuilt in a manner the Gods favor, and there\u2019s no guarantee that all of them would survive such an apocalypse anyway. While some of the pettiest Gods might not give a flying rat\u2019s ass about humanity, most of them will still be invested in their own survival at the very least.<br /> The problem with this argument is that it is based on the assumption, \u201cIf God A exists and is active in the world, then God A must also do X, Y, and Z in the world.\u201d If Zeus strikes a mortal with a thunderbolt for insulting him, then any other mortal that insults him must also be struck by a thunderbolt. It assumes that the Gods can\u2019t change over time. It assumes that they don\u2019t learn from their past experiences. The Gods are people. They have their own desires and plans, and most probably don\u2019t include being hopelessly Fatebound among them. Avoiding that requires a degree of subtlety.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T23:03:46-07:00","id":1237697,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">&quot;To the people asking for a wildly different history of the World; why the binary? Why \u201cmust\u201d divine influence change either everything so that the World is nothing like the world we know? \u201cObviously it must be so\u201d goes the argument, but people showed how it isn\u2019t. What\u2019s the logic behind, other than wanting to play a High Fantasy setting in a game geared for Urban Fantasy?&quot;<br /> I didn't say &quot;it MUST be so, only that I felt it should. But how do you figure that Gods and their Children is limited to Urban Fantasy?</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T23:06:54-07:00","id":1237698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1236881-thoughts-on-the-world?p=1237693#post1237693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem with this argument is that it is based on the assumption, \u201cIf God A exists and is active in the world, then God A must also do X, Y, and Z in the world.\u201d If Zeus strikes a mortal with a thunderbolt for insulting him, then any other mortal that insults him must also be struck by a thunderbolt. It assumes that the Gods can\u2019t change over time. It assumes that they don\u2019t learn from their past experiences. .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Uranus - I'm going to devour my own children out of fear that they might overthrow me some day.<br /> <br /> Cronus - I'm going to castrate my father and take over his position. Then I'm going to devour my children out of fear that they might overthrow me some day.<br /> <br /> Zeus - I'm going to castrate my father and take over his position. Then I'm going to devour my own child out of fear that they might overthrow me some day.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I can't help but notice a recurring pattern here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> But I'll agree with the idea that divine interference could be responsible for YHVH's shift in personality over the years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T23:20:49-07:00","id":1237701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1236881-thoughts-on-the-world?p=1237697#post1237697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">&quot;To the people asking for a wildly different history of the World; why the binary? Why \u201cmust\u201d divine influence change either everything so that the World is nothing like the world we know? \u201cObviously it must be so\u201d goes the argument, but people showed how it isn\u2019t. What\u2019s the logic behind, other than wanting to play a High Fantasy setting in a game geared for Urban Fantasy?&quot;<br /> I didn't say &quot;it MUST be so, only that I felt it should. But how do you figure that Gods and their Children is limited to Urban Fantasy?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I think it might have something to do with the trope that in every story that features modern times, but with the presence of supernatural, it always, always involves the supernatural having gone into hiding. The Gods have some kind of pact or some other explanation that forbids them from directly interfering with mortal affairs. The power of magic waned over time as people came to embrace the ways of science, or maybe humans just outright hunted monsters to the brink of extinction.<br /> <br /> Scion 2E is the first story I've come across that assumes the Gods, Magic and Monsters never kept a low profile, but rather maintained a recognized presence throughout history. They aren't returning to the World after a long period of absence. They've been active in the World the entire time, and we should expect that the World is different because of it.<br /> <br /> I'm sure everybody here is familiar with the Butterfly Effect. Altering history isn't as cut and dry as just changing one little event, your changing every event that follows the initial change, unleashing a chain reaction that ripples throughout time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T00:08:06-07:00","id":1237705,"title":"","content":"I'm confused...where does it say the history of the World is the same as ours? It said it resembles ours, sure, but that is not the same.n Cortez showed up?<br /> <br /> The MCU resembles our universe, the World of Darkness also looks like our and so does American Gods and the Wicked and the Divine. But they can't have the same history because of the vast differences between them, let alone the conceits not present in our own.<br /> <br /> The fact is resembling our history doesn't mean they share it. It means the outlines look the same if you squint, that maybe at first glance you don't notice the drive through is O'Toolies, not Mc'Donalds because they don't look that different until you go beyond the surface.<br /> Why isn't the Church of Thor bigger in Marvel comics? It is; but that isn't where the spotlight is and it hasn't overwhelmed the other faiths.<br /> <br /> Why isn't the World more different from our own? It is; you just have to shine the light there; it is just close enough that the World looks the same at first glance, if you squint.<br /> So look closer, dig deeper and explore the 'mythic underground'. Ask the questions and come up with the answers. Why didn't the Theoi fight to maintain their control of the Roman Empire? What ever happened to the Holy Grail and King Arthur? Where were the Teotl when Cortez showed up?<br /> <br /> These are good questions, but the answers should exist in the World and should be found out at the table.<br /> <br /> The World is different; but you have to look for those differences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 07-22-2018, 09:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T23:45:11-07:00","id":1237900,"title":"","content":"I think that was the point - the world <i>should </i>be different. Some say a little, some say a lot. I'm just one of those who feels it should be much more different than the default, but that's my personal bias.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T11:38:24-07:00","id":1238021,"title":"","content":"I can see both sides, to be honest. Both have their issues. The Masquerade has its obvious logistical issues, but making big changes to earth's history comes with its problems too. It can lead to unpredictable, butterfly effect style results, and end up with a world that barely resembles ours. That to me essentially defies the purpose of an urban fantasy story, turning it into high fantasy in a world very loosely based on hours. If that's what you want, more power to you, but between the two extremes I would prefer a Masquerade, with all the logistical problems essentially being acceptable breaks from reality. This sort of middle ground is honestly kind of an alien concept to me. I understand why people think the gods being real would lead to enormous changes, far bigger than described in the material, but at the same time, I don't really want it to go too far away from the urban fantasy feel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T14:26:06-07:00","id":1238055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1236881-thoughts-on-the-world?p=1238021#post1238021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see both sides, to be honest. Both have their issues. The Masquerade has its obvious logistical issues, but making big changes to earth's history comes with its problems too. It can lead to unpredictable, butterfly effect style results, and end up with a world that barely resembles ours. That to me essentially defies the purpose of an urban fantasy story, turning it into high fantasy in a world very loosely based on hours. If that's what you want, more power to you, but between the two extremes I would prefer a Masquerade, with all the logistical problems essentially being acceptable breaks from reality. This sort of middle ground is honestly kind of an alien concept to me. I understand why people think the gods being real would lead to enormous changes, far bigger than described in the material, but at the same time, I don't really want it to go too far away from the urban fantasy feel.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> In order for a Masquerade to work, most of the population has to agree to make it work. And considering the Titans are god-level beings who have come to embody their purviews in their purest form, with entire species worth of monsters devoted to serving them, I think that would be near impossible to achieve. And i<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">f mortals have known about the existence of the supernatural all this time, then it stands to reason they've come up with a few ways to protect themselves over the ages.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> Which is why I think the idea of the supernatural creatures choosing to live on the fringes of society makes the most logical sense. The World knows that fairies, nymphs, satyrs and talking animals exists, but they prefer to stay within the comfort of their sacred forests. If you happen to run across one, it's probably because you went actively looking for one. Unless there's an emergency that forces them to venture into more civilized lands.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Cities protect themselves against vampire attacks by instituting a curfew in which nobody but the proper authorities are supposed to be on the streets after a certain hour.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> People might be required to submit themselves to a lycanthropy screening after a body is discovered to have been mauled by some unidentified animal.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for dangerous cultists... well, I suppose the government would deal with them the say way they do in the real world","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T16:59:10-07:00","id":1238090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1236881-thoughts-on-the-world?p=1237698#post1237698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Uranus - I'm going to devour my own children out of fear that they might overthrow me some day.<br /> <br /> Cronus - I'm going to castrate my father and take over his position. Then I'm going to devour my children out of fear that they might overthrow me some day.<br /> <br /> Zeus - I'm going to castrate my father and take over his position. Then I'm going to devour my own child out of fear that they might overthrow me some day.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I can't help but notice a recurring pattern here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>But there are differences showing that gods learn. Uranus didn't devour his children, he imprisoned them thus making it possible for Gaia to support them. Cronus devoured his children to stop that from happening. Zeus on the other hand is much more careful in his actions with his children, only ever acting if the said child was prophesied to be a threat, thus causing him to swallow Metis before she could give birth to her second child thus stopping that before there was even a chance and also arranging to marriage between Thetis and Pelias for similar reasons since it was prophesied that Thetis child would surpass his father. Other then that tho Zeus has been far less dictorial then the previous kings of the world, mostly because he doesn't wish to follow his predecessors mistakes and fall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T12:00:17-07:00","id":1239391,"title":"","content":"I haven't received my copy, so I don't know if this has been adressed. <br /> <br /> I believe one of the core concept to define from the World is the relation between mortals and gods. The first edition was pretty vague in this regard, only stating that fate binded the gods. When my campaign reached demi-god and god, I had to answer the question: Why do gods care or need the humans? Why is the World particularly important to Gods and Titans? Why can't they intervene directly on the World?<br /> <br /> Answering these will probably solve your problem altogether. In my campaign I balanced the metaphysics of it all. The fundamentals of the universe were like a tapestry. These raw concepts were the Titans, their children subdivisions of the concept (ex: Fire would have aspects of Hearth, Heat, Creativity, etc...). The gods were the children of the Titans that ripped free from their parents, stealing part of this 'tapestry' with them. The Titans as fundamental forces wanted to be whole again. Enter the humans. While the divine are the building blocks of creation, mortals were collectively the embodiment of 'Will', blowing their stories through Fate to the Gods and Titans. It's what drives change, movement through the threads of the tapestry. The less they were to remember the stories of the gods, Fate's shackles would become weaker. The Wyrd would then reinitiate the cycle, to bolster it's claim on new legends. <br /> <br /> This is why claiming the World or it's fundamental Will was critical to the struggle of the Titans. Controlling or corrupting the Will of the universe could win the war unto itself. Is the Will a fundamental, a Titan itself, or is it something else? How many cycles has the World been through? That's for the players to find out <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> So per say the gods don't need the human's prayers and it also helps to explains the Wyrd. It can also explains why the Gods would battle to protect or claim soverainty over the World, even the most selfish ones. I found that this enquiry to the metaphysics of the Scion universe helped to keep intrigue flowing even at God levels instead of having just concluding the Ragnarok epic battles. <br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> So to get back to the issue at hand, if the gods have never left the World, there has to be a reason. Why aren't they more present? Have they stayed away from major events in human history, keeping their conflicts as hidden as possible to avoid implicating / fatebinding with mortals? I would also argue that otherwise some of them would be deeply invested in the fate of humans and while picturing a Scion behind major conflicts of History is cool, I always feel awkward to appoint a God-parent to historical figures, as if humans couldn't be great and terrible on their own.<br /> <br /> Other questions: <br /> <br /> Does it 'cost' them something to sire Scions? With satellites signaling the end of any Terra Incognita, how or why are there still creatures in the World? Is there a truce between pantheons, a sort of NATO / UN in regard to the Titan threat? If so, are Scions the ones to manage these or are the Divine can't help meddling? <br /> <br /> If this isn't adressed in Origins, I hope they do in Hero. It's easy to disregard and say: it is what it is. But the answers shape the relation between the Scion with it's parent, the World, other Scions, etc... These are fundamentals to the story and character development.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24447-catabase","name":"Catabase","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T12:37:40-07:00","id":1239405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Catabase</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1236881-thoughts-on-the-world?p=1239391#post1239391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't received my copy, so I don't know if this has been adressed.<br /> <br /> I believe one of the core concept to define from the World is the relation between mortals and gods. The first edition was pretty vague in this regard, only stating that fate binded the gods. When my campaign reached demi-god and god, I had to answer the question: Why do gods care or need the humans? Why is the World particularly important to Gods and Titans? Why can't they intervene directly on the World?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Titans need the World because they are the living embodiments of universal concepts. Terra wasn't just the Greater Titan of the World, she was the very concept of The World itself. Muspelheim wasn't just the Greater Titan of Fire, he was the very concept of fire given consciousness.<br /> <br /> Gods, on the other hand, came to embody aspects of mortal concepts such as law, chaos, wisdom, love and so on. The Gods are recognized by their distinctly human characteristics, while the Titans are recognized by their more primal natures and impartial attitudes. The Titans aren't explicitly malicious, they're just behaving in accordance with what their nature drives them to do. And if somebody happens to get hurt along the way, that's just how life goes.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for directly intervening with the world, they actually can. In fact, mythology is rife with stories of them doing exactly that. It was only the work of popular modern media who began to implement rules and systems that prevented the Gods from taking an active hand over our development.<br /> <br /> As for the Scion setting, you have the concept of Fate Bonds, in which the Gods (and presumably Titans) are subject to the will of predetermination, as well as mortal comprehension. If a God behaves like an arrogant prick, then Fate will conspire to place them in situations where they continue to behave like an arrogant prick.<br /> <br /> And in 1E, there's a possible story hook that revolves around changing humanity's perception of Aten (the Titan of Light) by trapping him inside the Hadron Collider and changing the way mortals viewed his existence. If the plan worked, then Aten's consciousness dissolves as he becomes nothing more than a mass of photons spinning around in a giant tube.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-27-2018, 03:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T12:19:52-07:00","id":1239754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Catabase</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1236881-thoughts-on-the-world?p=1239391#post1239391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So to get back to the issue at hand, if the gods have never left the World, there has to be a reason. Why aren't they more present? Have they stayed away from major events in human history, keeping their conflicts as hidden as possible to avoid implicating / fatebinding with mortals? I would also argue that otherwise some of them would be deeply invested in the fate of humans and while picturing a Scion behind major conflicts of History is cool, I always feel awkward to appoint a God-parent to historical figures, as if humans couldn't be great and terrible on their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the World of 2e, the Gods get involved with the World's affairs quite often. Just y'know subtle-like. Rather than Ares appearing and demolishing an army (which can lead to MASS Fatebinding which is capable of fundamentally shattering or reshaping a God's identity, see what happened to the Orisha and the Loa) he may provide a blessing to an army, making them fight better. Sometimes they <i>do</i> walk the World, clad in human forms called Incarnations, helping advance their goals and agendas.<br /> <br /> There <i>are</i> a couple of historical figures who are Scions in the World. Iulius Caesar, for one, was a Scion of Aphrodite and his conquest of the Gauls was part of a power play to try and guarantee his Apotheosis. Imhotep was a Scion in 1e and I believe he still is. There's a college in Memphis, Egypt, that bears his name. You <i>are</i> right in that not <i>every</i> historical figure needs to be a Scion, and Neall himself has said in the Discord that he'd rather not say EVERYONE important in history was a Scion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does it 'cost' them something to sire Scions? </div> </div> </div>Time. Effort. They'll also have to get Birthrights arranged should they choose a Visitation. Scions are a hefty investment... But not to the degree that you may be thinking, where if Re has a Scion the sun is going to be a bit dimmer for a bit while he recovers.<br /> <br /> And unless it's part of their legend, most Godly Incarnations aren't going to have a whole litter of kids. Very rarely does something come of them laying with a human. Even rarer are the ones who become full Scions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With satellites signaling the end of any Terra Incognita, how or why are there still creatures in the World? </div> </div> </div>The thing about Terra Incognita is that they're tough to pin down. Take a turn down the forest road, you'll find yourself near a lake that isn't on any map YOU own.<br /> <br /> That said, it's not like the people of The World are <i>ignorant</i> about these creatures. Many in Greece know that yeah, centaurs run wild somewhere over there-ish. Most people just don't go looking for them because, well, centaurs are brutish, mean, territorial, and hooooo <i>boy</i> they are mean to intruders let me tell you. I think the Origin book mentions that there's like, Troll Preserves over in Norway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is there a truce between pantheons, a sort of NATO / UN in regard to the Titan threat? If so, are Scions the ones to manage these or are the Divine can't help meddling? </div> </div> </div>Actually, depending on whom you ask, the different Gods have different outlooks on the whole Titan War thing. The Deva, Teotl, and Theoi are the end of the spectrum going &quot;Man we gotta get rid of ALL the Titans! They're <i>dangerous</i>!&quot; while at the other end you have the Manitou, who are all &quot;God? Titan? Man, everything's just a spirit. Some can be <b>jerks</b>, sure-&quot; and the Orisha, who just go &quot;Titans? Psh, I doubt they're different enough to warrant a different name.&quot;<br /> <br /> However, when monsters threaten the World on a smaller scale, usually a Hero Scion is the one dispersed. They have a great deal more operational freedom, and they have the advantage of being relatively precise compared to the full wrath of the Deva.<br /> <br /> Now for the relationships between the Pantheons... MOST generally don't engage in full war with one-another. Generally. Mostly due to worry of mutually assured destruction. You may get proxy fronts, power plays, bits of influence shifting here and there through omens, messages granted to followers and temples, and maybe having a Scion make a play against a rival God.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}